664 998 Q 1574 998 1574 1101 L 1568 3693 Q 1568 3744 1587 3760 Q 1606 3776 1645 3776 L 1920 3776 Q 1997 3776 1997 3718 L 2003 1062 Q 2003 998 1939 998 L 1664 998 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" d=\"M 2362 4806 Q 2605 4806 2797 4755 Q 2989 4704 3142 4614 Q 3296 4525 3414 4416 Q 3533 4307 3610 4186 Q 3622 4160 3625 4131 Q 3629 4102 3590 4083 L 3226 3936 Q 3194 3917 3168 3933 Q 3142 3949 3130 3974 Q 2989 4141 2813 4243 Q 2637 4346 2368 4346 Q 1907 4346 1609 4122 Q 1312 3898 1171 3510 Q 1030 3123 1030 2637 Q 1030 2534 1049 2502 Q 1069 2470 1146 2509 Q 1389 2630 1670 2732 Q 1952 2835 2330 2835 Q 2822 2835 3171 2652 Q 3520 2470 3702 2156 Q 3885 1843 3885 1446 Q 3885 998 3664 656 Q 3443 314 3068 128 Q 2694 -58 2234 -58 Q 1670 -58 1264 220 Q 858 499 640 1027 Q 422 1555 422 2304 Q 422 3085 656 3645 Q 890 4205 1325 4505 Q 1760 4806 2362 4806 L 2362 4806 z\nM 2259 2387 Q 2093 2387 1885 2345 Q 1677 2304 1491 2240 Q 1306 2176 1171 2093 Q 1094 2042 1068 1987 Q 1043 1933 1043 1818 Q 1043 1587 1116 1340 Q 1190 1094 1334 876 Q 1478 659 1702 524 Q 1926 390 2234 390 Q 2534 390 2768 524 Q 3002 659 3139 896 Q 3277 1133 3277 1421 Q 3277 1690 3155 1910 Q 3034 2131 2803 2259 Q 2573 2387 2259 2387 L 2259 2387 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e2\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(121.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(142.703125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(323.48205 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" d=\"M 2470 4678 Q 2502 4717 2534 4733 Q 2566 4749 2630 4749 L 3059 4749 Q 3136 4749 3136 4672 L 3136 1792 Q 3136 1734 3187 1734 L 3789 1734 Q 3878 1734 3878 1670 L 3878 1357 Q 3878 1274 3789 1274 L 3194 1274 Q 3136 1274 3136 1210 L 3136 96 Q 3136 0 3034 0 L 2598 0 Q 2515 0 2515 83 L 2515 1229 Q 2515 1274 2458 1274 L 384 1274 Q 288 1274 288 1357 L 288 1683 Q 288 1728 313 1776 Q 339 1824 390 1894 L 2470 4678 L 2470 4678 z\nM 2445 1734 Q 2502 1734 2502 1779 L 2502 3910 Q 2502 3987 2483 3993 Q 2464 4000 2413 3936 L 851 1818 Q 787 1734 896 1734 L 2445 1734 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e2\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(148.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(169.609375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pa78de7c80f\"><rect x=\"47.558\" y=\"11.270471\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Annual operating profit by utilisation ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Profit = 20kt × utilisation × $1,800 − $21M.</p> <ul><li>50%: <b>−$3.0M</b>, payback —</li><li>75%: <b>+$6.0M</b>, payback 15.0 years</li><li>90%: <b>+$11.4M</b>, payback 7.9 years</li></ul> <p>Break-even utilisation: $21M ÷ (20kt × $1,800) = <b>58%</b>.</p> <p>To pay back in eight years the plant must earn $11.25M a year, which needs <b>90% utilisation</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> only near-full running meets the hurdle; at 75% payback takes 15 years, and at 50% the plant loses money.</p>"},{"q":"Only 45% of capacity is contracted. What does that tell you, and what would you do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Contracted volume alone (45%) is below the 58% break-even: the plant would lose money on signed contracts only.</p> <ul><li>Sign more <b>long-term supply contracts</b> with battery factories and carmakers before committing the full $90M</li> <li><b>Build in phases</b>: a first line sized to contracted volume, then expand</li> <li><b>Offer gate-fee discounts</b> for multi-year commitments</li> <li><b>Hedge metal prices</b> partly, since lithium and nickel prices swing sharply</li></ul>"},{"q":"What risks would you raise with the board?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Metal prices: a fall in lithium or nickel cuts the $1,800 margin per tonne</li><li>Battery chemistry: newer batteries use less cobalt and nickel, so they're worth less to recycle</li> <li>Timing: car batteries reach end of life slowly, so the plant depends on factory scrap for years</li><li>Competition for scrap from other European recyclers</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't build the full plant yet. It needs 58% utilisation to break even and about 90% to pay back within eight years, yet only 45% of capacity is under contract; at 75% it would take 15 years to pay back. I recommend building in phases sized to contracted volume and signing long-term supply deals before adding capacity. Risk: metal price swings change the margin per tonne. Next step: approach the three largest battery factories in the Nordics for multi-year supply agreements.","great":["Recognises utilisation drives profit in a fixed-cost plant","Compares contracted volume with break-even","Proposes phasing to reduce risk","Raises metal-price and chemistry risks"],"id":42,"slug":"northcairn-recycling"}